# vNext Skill: execute-step

## Default runtime role

runtime_role: assistance/v1

Follow `.workflow-system/WORKFLOW_PROTOCOL.md` and the management API in
`.workflow-system/runtime/support/ASSISTANCE_API.md`. Use the native service:
`node .workflow-system/runtime/support/assistance.mjs <command> --root <project>`.
Source-repository equivalent: `node runtime/vnext/support/assistance.mjs`.

Use `context`/`find`/`read` for current and historical sources, `snapshot` for an
explicit optional file capture, and `record` for facts and decisions. A malformed
active task, stale evidence, missing review, old receipt or failed index is not a
development gate. Record actual outcomes without obtaining a preflight or repairing
legacy state. Existing capability/transaction metadata lists optional compatible
tools, not mandatory calls. Do not use run-entry recovery as a prerequisite.

If a management operation fails, preserve its actual error and any output already
saved; use another authorized recording method when available and continue
independent authorized work. Do not retry unchanged calls, rerun business commands,
invent IDs/PASS or claim persistence succeeded. Ask only about a genuinely unresolved
user choice or unavailable business prerequisite, not an internal gate code.

## Method

Establish the current requested work and actual scope from the user's instruction,
existing plan and source. Runtime state is context, not permission. Read relevant
requirements, contracts, past findings and tests. An optional snapshot can preserve
before-state; failure to obtain it does not require preflight recovery to edit code.

Implement the authorized work and necessary local corrections. Do not expand into
unrelated work, touch excluded paths, fabricate user authorization or infer writes
from discovery alone. Ask when a real scope/goal choice is unresolved, not when a
Runtime map, quota, receipt, plan revision or status disagrees.

Run only the authorized, necessary validation. Keep actual selectors, commands,
outputs, source versions, failures and not-run checks. Do not add persistent tests
or full-suite/E2E runs merely to satisfy a workflow record. Save an `execution`
and/or `test-run` observation even when results fail, plans changed or links cannot
be resolved. Never change failed to passed to satisfy a completion condition.

Implementation self-check is normal work, not a formal review. By default do not
create a new formal review, including via record-review-result. An existing explicit
instruction covering execution AND review may be completed in this interaction;
follow review-change methods and call it self-review when the implementer reviews.
Do not claim independent review. Existing real reviews may be referenced without
manufacturing a new one. Record the actual outcome and remaining work; no mandatory
complete-executed-step or complete-reviewed-step call is needed to continue.

## Result

Return the actual requested result, affected scope, evidence/record references,
remaining work and any unsaved/unreconciled data. Preserve existing user decisions
and exclusions; an explicit read-only request remains read-only. A record's successful
write does not certify the product or expand authorization.

`next_route` is a recommendation, not the only allowed next action. Default to stopping
after the requested work; a still-effective explicit instruction can cover further
stages in the same interaction. Never invent such an instruction from a test PASS or
Runtime suggestion. Do not automatically widen validation or perform unrequested external effects.

